---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase, ownerName, ownerBio, inquiryLabel } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Quiet Compass" description="The point of view behind Quiet Compass: useful questions, clear decisions and honest evidence. An independent digital studio sharing original concept studies." route="C03">
 <section><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">C03 / About the practice</span><h1>Good design<br/>makes room for people.</h1></div><p>Quiet Compass is an independent digital studio in development. This portfolio shares self-initiated studies in strategy, identity, product design and the web.</p></div><p class="about-statement">The ambition is simple: make the next step easier to understand, without sanding all the character out of the experience.</p>{ownerName&&<div class="honesty"><h2>{ownerName}</h2>{ownerBio&&<p>{ownerBio}</p>}</div>}<p class="measure muted">The projects here are concepts, not a disguised client list. Their artifacts are real work created for this portfolio; their sample data is synthetic. They show a way of thinking and make its assumptions available for inspection.</p></div></section>
 <section class="method-section"><div class="shell"><span class="route">A working point of view</span><div class="principle-grid"><article><h2>Ask before polishing.</h2><p>What is someone trying to decide? What do they already know? Where could they reasonably get stuck? Start there, rather than with a visual effect.</p></article><article><h2>Explain the tradeoff.</h2><p>A smaller menu can hide useful choices. A shorter form can ask for too little. A strong direction makes its compromises explicit.</p></article><article><h2>Leave room to disagree.</h2><p>An inspectable prototype is more useful than a confident adjective. Show the alternatives, invite questions and revise the parts that do not hold up.</p></article><article><h2>Care about the ordinary visit.</h2><p>The narrow phone, the keyboard, the slow connection and the return visit are part of the design—not exceptions to it.</p></article></div></div></section>
 <section><div class="shell section-head"><div><span class="route">Working together</span><h2>A useful conversation<br/>starts with the constraint.</h2></div><div><p>The project-brief page asks about the people, the current difficulty and the outcome you have in mind. Delivery availability is stated before you start; a local copy can be saved without sending anything.</p><a class="btn" href={withBase('contact/')}>{inquiryLabel} →</a><p class="small"><a class="text-link" href={withBase('colophon/')}>Looking for the technical system? Read the colophon.</a></p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
